- comparisons:[
-  ['Song China','Examinations and appointed officials','Confucian ethics and Buddhist traditions','Agriculture, markets, taxes, and manufactures','Bureaucratic continuity alongside commercial growth.'],
-  ['Dar al-Islam','Multiple sultanates and dynasties','Islam, with Christian and Jewish communities','Farming, cities, commerce, and scholarly patronage','Shared practices connected politically divided territories.'],
-  ['South and Southeast Asia','Sultanates, regional kingdoms, and maritime states','Hinduism, Buddhism, Islam, Bhakti, and Sufism','Irrigation, land revenue, ports, and shipping','Cultural influence did not require a single regional empire.'],
-  ['The Americas','Maya cities, Mexica tributaries, and Inca administration','Sacred kingship and diverse local traditions','Tribute, labor obligations, intensive farming','States mobilized resources through different institutions.'],
-  ['Africa','Mali, Ethiopia, Great Zimbabwe, and independent cities','Islam, Christianity, and indigenous traditions','Agriculture, pastoralism, crafts, and trade','Centralized and decentralized systems coexisted.'],
-  ['Europe','Monarchies, nobles, city-states, and church authorities','Christianity alongside Jewish and Muslim communities','Manors, free and coerced labor, and growing markets','Regional variation complicates a single “feudal Europe” model.']
